			<div class="content" id="post-content-2136285">
									

<p>Peppers, you wrote a human being dehumanized by the Foundation who has learned to perfectly dehumanize other human beings and use them as parts of a game.</p>
<p>I love you. +1</p>
<p>However, things:</p>
<ul>
<li>The stick handlers (&quot;supervisors&quot;) are mind-wiped once; never again?</li>
<li>The stick handlers are mind-wiped; does this mean your Foundation has a way to erase episodic memory without affecting semantic and procedural memories? That is: forget their previous lives, not their previous capacities and whatever they learnt back then? If so, we have to develop the tech bubbles behind it. &lt;3</li>
<li>The stick handlers are brought into a building, right; what if there is an underwater building, or a subterranean anomaly, or an anomaly inside a reality-unstable or otherwise tricky location? Do they send D-Class Prelim teams there, or default to Class E and MTFs?</li>
</ul>
<p>Thanks in advance for sharing this. :3</p>

