			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2136396">
									

<p>If a criminal has their memory erased, how do you continue treating them like a criminal? What's even the point at that point beyond torturing basically an entirely new person for the crimes of someone else?<br />
This exact thing was handled beautifully in an episode of Babylon 5 <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Passing_through_Gethsemane">&quot;Passing through Gethsemane&quot;</a> and the way it's handled here under a veneer of humor is juzt way too distracting and sickening for me to get past</p>

