			<div class="content" id="post-content-2136415">
									

<p>Selfishly copying here what I said just a comment away:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The stick handlers are mind-wiped; does this mean your Foundation has a way to erase episodic memory without affecting semantic and procedural memories? That is: forget their previous lives, not their previous capacities and whatever they learnt back then? If so, we have to develop the tech bubbles behind it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Different memories have different functions. While heavily connected to each other, memories can remain detached.</p>

